From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: meanaverage <18336095+meanaverage@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:02:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(egfx): track only the surfaces the compositor can hold

The compositor refuses a surface larger than 16384 pixels on either edge
(MAX_SURFACE_DIM), but the client recorded it anyway: in its surfaces,
and, with an external H.264 decoder, in the sizes that bound a frame's
regions. A server could create a 65535x65535 surface and send H.264 to
it: each frame was handed to the decoder, its regions clipped to a size
no pixels were allocated for, decoded, read back, and then dropped.
Re-creating an existing surface that large did more: the compositor
returned before removing the surface it replaced, so the old one stayed
mapped and drew the commands meant for the new one, while the client
took the id for 65535x65535.

Client and compositor now share the compositor's limit
(Compositor::holds_surface). A CreateSurface beyond it leaves no surface
under its id on either side, and the surface it replaces goes with it:
commands for the id fail as they do for any unknown surface. The limit
itself is unchanged; 16384 is twice the width of an 8K display. A
surface the compositor's byte budget refuses is still tracked, as
before.

The fuzzing oracle that mirrors the client's surface state follows.
